note tests/look-home.om: drives look-home.om on the C harness's schedule (~/work/IMacLook/home/harness.c) and writes
note the same regions as P6 PPMs to fd 1, in the harness's order: flashA flashB barA barB wordsC barC wordsD barD.
note NIGHT's hole radius at the two flash frames is taken from the C harness log (346/417 at 1280, 1066/1285 at 3840).
note stdin: the harness's <name>-night.ppm files, in that order (the bare night each frame is drawn on).
note Unit: font-data.om font.om look-paint.om look-night.om look-mind.om look-home.om tio.om tests/look-home.om.
global Tbg uchar 16384
global Thead ulong 4
global Tnow long 1
text Tsay "Opening the Allen repository on GitHub, aien-dev/aienux. The same code runs on the Spark, so ask me about any file."
text Ttyped "open allen github repository"
note reads exactly n bytes from fd 0 into Tbg
fn tfill n ulong to void
got = ulong 0
while lt got n
r = read 0 Tbg got sub n got
if le r 0
trap 2
end
got = add got ulong r
end
end
note one P6 header: "P6\n<w> <h>\n255\n" read byte by byte; Thead 1 2 = w h
fn thead to void
nl = ulong 0
v = ulong 0
k = ulong 0
while lt nl 4
tfill 1
c = get Tbg 0
if or eq c 10 eq c 32
if ne k 0
put Thead nl v
nl = add nl 1
end
v = 0
k = 0
else
if ge c 48
v = add mul v 10 sub ulong c 48
k = add k 1
end
end
end
end
note one P6 from fd 0 into Nfrm (the frame's size must match Lg 0 1)
fn tpx p ulong to ulong
c = shl ulong get Tbg p 16
c = or c shl ulong get Tbg add p 1 8
ret or c ulong get Tbg add p 2
end
fn trow at ulong w ulong to void
for i ulong w
put Nfrm add at i uint tpx mul i 3
end
end
fn tload to void
thead
w = get Thead 1
for j ulong get Thead 2
tfill mul w 3
trow mul j w w
end
end
fn tpix c ulong to void
tc uchar and shr c 16 255
tc uchar and shr c 8 255
tc uchar and c 255
end
fn tprow at ulong w ulong to void
for i ulong w
tpix ulong get Nfrm add at i
end
end
fn tppm x long y long w long h long to void
tc 80
tc 54
tc 10
tu ulong w
tc 32
tu ulong h
tc 10
tu 255
tc 10
at = add mul ulong y ulong get Lg 0 ulong x
for j ulong ulong h
tprow at ulong w
at = add at ulong get Lg 0
end
end
fn trun upto long to void
while le get Tnow 0 upto
hmstep get Tnow 0
put Tnow 0 add get Tnow 0 16
end
end
note draws the frame last stepped on the bare night from stdin, and writes the region
fn tdump x long y long w long h long to void
tload
hmflash 0 0 get Lg 0 get Lg 1
hmtext 0 0 get Lg 0 get Lg 1
tppm x y w h
end
note the regions the C harness dumps: the flash box, the bar box (Hm 28..31) and the words box of lay_out
fn tflash to void
r = add shr hmfrad get Hm 12 4 2
x = sub get Lg 3 r
y = sub get Lg 4 r
r = add mul 2 r 1
tppm x y r r
end
fn tbar to void
tppm get Hm 28 get Hm 29 get Hm 30 get Hm 31
end
fn twords to void
x = sub sub get Lg 3 hms 450 hms 8
y = sub add get Lg 4 hms 250 hms 34
w = add hms 900 hms 16
h = add mul 5 hms 40 hms 30
tppm x y w h
end
fn tdraw to void
hmflash 0 0 get Lg 0 get Lg 1
hmtext 0 0 get Lg 0 get Lg 1
end
fn main to long
note the first night file gives the size (all frames share it): Lg 0 1 are only placeholders for its load
put Lg 0 1280
put Lg 1 800
tload
put Lg 0 long get Thead 1
put Lg 1 long get Thead 2
kw = div mul get Lg 0 256 1920
kh = div mul get Lg 1 256 1080
put Lg 2 pkmin kw kh
put Lg 3 div get Lg 0 2
put Lg 4 div mul get Lg 1 40 100
pkinit
hminit
put Tnow 0 0
put Nthol 0 1
put Nthole 0 add mul get Lg 3 16 8
put Nthole 1 add mul get Lg 4 16 8
trun 12100
put Nthole 3 346
if ne get Lg 0 1280
put Nthole 3 1066
end
tdraw
tflash
trun 12290
put Nthole 3 417
if ne get Lg 0 1280
put Nthole 3 1285
end
tload
tdraw
tflash
put Nthol 0 0
trun 16500
tload
tdraw
tbar
for i ulong len Ttyped
hmkey ulong get Ttyped i
trun add get Tnow 0 120
end
tload
tdraw
tbar
trun 20500
hmkey 13
hmthink 1
trun 23500
for i ulong len Tsay
put Hmsay i get Tsay i
end
put Hmsayn 0 len Tsay
hmsaid
speak = add get Tnow 0 400
n = long len Tsay
trun add speak div mul n 35 2
tload
tdraw
twords
tload
tdraw
tbar
trun add add speak mul n 35 500
tload
tdraw
twords
tload
tdraw
tbar
tflush
ret 0
end
